      "translation": {
        "english_text": "Pity! If they had looked at pity, many frogs could never have seen mansions and lofty towers! Look at Malayappan! How did he get this luxuriant life? Because he never even thought of pity! Defeat is the first step laid toward victory! If you are to get Kumaran, Kumaran must forget Meenu. Meenu thinks Kumaran is dead.... We must not let Kumaran outside! No one else must know Kumaran is alive! Understand? At least in this, be careful!",
        "mode": "prose-faithful",
        "notes": [
          "`மண்டூகங்கள்` is retained as the source's frog image rather than replacing the satire with a smoother abstraction."
        ]
      }
